.TH NIXUP 1 "" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nixup \- NixOS update utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nixup
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIFLAGS\fR]
.br
.B nixup help
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBnixup\fR is an integrated NixOS management CLI that wraps \fBnix\fR commands
with build isolation, automatic logging, lock-file strategy, and package
recovery logic.
.PP
All builds are performed in an isolated \fI.build/\fR directory (physical copy,
no git tracking) and invoked with \fBpath:\fR mode to enable testing of
uncommitted changes.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B os
Build and activate NixOS system configuration (default when no subcommand is given).
.TP
.B home
Build and activate Home Manager configuration.
.TP
.B check
Run code integrity checks in order: deadnix, statix fix, alejandra,
shellcheck, nix eval. With \fB--deep\fR, replaces nix eval with nix flake check
to validate all hosts.
.TP
.B update
Update flake.lock inputs. Rolling hosts update \fI.locks/_rolling.lock\fR;
stable hosts update \fI.locks/<hostname>.lock\fR.
.TP
.B clean
Delete old Nix generations to free disk space.
Default: user home profile only, keep last 3 generations.
.TP
.B iso
Build a custom installation ISO image. Result is symlinked into \fI.build/\fR.
.TP
.B fix
Search for the last working commit of a broken unstable package and pin it
to \fI.env\fR. Reference the pinned package as \fBunstable-fallback.<pkgName>\fR
in \fI*.nix\fR files.
.TP
.B help
Show help. Pass a subcommand name to see subcommand-specific help.
.SH FLAGS
.SS os / home
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-build
Build only; do not create a new generation or activate.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-try
Activate immediately without registering a new generation.
Reverts on reboot.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-stage
Schedule activation for the next boot.
.SS check
.TP
.B \-\-deep
Replace \fBnix eval\fR with \fBnix flake check\fR to validate all hosts.
Note: does not update NIXUP_LAST_HOST.
.SS clean
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Include system profile (requires sudo) and run a full \fBnix-store --gc\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep= N
Number of generations to keep (default: 3).
Can be combined with \fB--all\fR.
.SS iso
.TP
.B \-\-arm
Build aarch64 target instead of the default x86_64.
.SS Global
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help. Use after a subcommand to see subcommand-specific help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Apply OS configuration to the current host:
.PP
.nf
    nixup
    nixup os
.fi
.PP
Build home configuration only:
.PP
.nf
    nixup home --build
.fi
.PP
Clean all old generations system-wide, keeping last 5:
.PP
.nf
    nixup clean --all --keep=5
.fi
.PP
Show subcommand help:
.PP
.nf
    nixup clean --help
    nixup help clean
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .env
Environment variables: NIXUP_LAST_HOST, NIX_UNSTABLE_FALLBACK_REV/SHA.
Located in the repository root.
.TP
.I .locks/
Per-host and rolling flake.lock files (\fI_rolling.lock\fR, \fI<hostname>.lock\fR).
.TP
.I /var/log/nixup/
Session logs (\fIYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.log\fR). Build logs (\fI*.nom-build.log\fR) are
kept only on failure and auto-deleted on success. Last 30 logs are retained.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nixos-rebuild (8),
.BR home-manager (1),
.BR nix (1)
